# ZeroOS: the image decides which services run (image/stage-zeroos/01-run.sh),
# so the first boot changes none of them.
#
# A card's first boot (/etc/machine-id says "uninitialized") makes systemd
# apply "presets" to every unit. Debian's presets turn on everything they
# don't name, which would bring back what the image turns off: adbd (a root
# shell on the USB port), Raspberry Pi's rename dialog on tty8,
# systemd-networkd beside NetworkManager, apt's daily jobs... On 0.9.4 that
# step ran while / was still read-only, so it changed nothing, but it left
# "Failed to populate /etc with preset unit settings" on the screen. With
# this rule first, it has nothing to do: no change and no message.
# (The machine ID stays "uninitialized": each card must make its own.)
disable *
